.TH modblockmap "1" "" "The scalpel3 Blockmap Modifier" "The scalpel3 Blockmap Modifier"

.SH NAME
modblockmap \- Manipulate existing scalpel3 blockmaps

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modblockmap
[\fB-j\fR \fIstart_block\fR]
[\fB-k\fR \fIend_block\fR]
img_filename
blockmap_filename
[0:block#] [1:block#] [?:block#]
[0:block#-block#] [1:block#-block#] [?:block#-block#]
[toolname tool_log_filename]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBmodblockmap\fR allows the user to cover (mark as used) or uncover (mark as available) single blocks or ranges of blocks within an existing scalpel3 blockmap. It also supports adjusting the active carve window and parsing logs from external tools (e.g., \fBphotorec\fR) to update coverage.
.PP
If only the image and blockmap filenames are provided, the current contents of the blockmap are displayed.
.PP
Changes are written back to the named blockmap; the image is not modified.
Options must precede the filenames. Block numbers start at zero and range
endpoints are inclusive. Quote query arguments, such as \fB'?:0-10'\fR,
to prevent the shell from treating \(oq?\(cq as a filename pattern.

.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.TP
.BI -j " start_block"
Set the start of the active carve window. Must be >= 0.

.TP
.BI -k " end_block"
Set the end of the active carve window. Must be >= 0.
.PP
An omitted endpoint retains its existing value. Both endpoints must be
within the image and the start must not exceed the end. Changing the window
recalculates duplicate and zero block information for that window.

.SH OPERATIONS
Operations are specified as positional arguments after the filenames.
.PP
.B Single Block Operations:
.br
\fB0:\fIblock\fR   - Uncover block.
.br
\fB1:\fIblock\fR   - Cover block.
.br
\fB?:\fIblock\fR   - Query block status.
.PP
.B Range Operations:
.br
\fB0:\fIstart\fR-\fIend\fR - Uncover range.
.br
\fB1:\fIstart\fR-\fIend\fR - Cover range.
.br
\fB?:\fIstart\fR-\fIend\fR - Query range status.
.PP
.B External Tool Integration:
.br
\fBphotorec\fR \fIlogfile\fR
.br
Parses a PhotoRec log file and covers blocks associated with files recovered by PhotoRec.
The log must contain the PhotoRec command line with its \fB/d\fR output
directory and recovery entries with inclusive block ranges. Range numbers
are used directly, so their block units must match the blockmap.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero after a successful query or update and nonzero on error.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scalpel3 (1),
.BR crblockmap (1),
.BR cmpblockmaps (1),
.BR blockmapfs (1),
.BR fragmentator (1)


